    "passives": {
      "CakePassiveAMarieAntoinette": {
        "id": "CakePassiveAMarieAntoinette",
        "found": true,
        "localization": {
          "name": "White Lily",
          "description": "After entering battle, this unit cannot be slept or poisoned for 50TU.\n\nUnless this unit is burning, this unit is immune to Stun effects, and cannot be immediately defeated without damage by a non-boss enemy.\n\nThe first time this unit defeats an enemy with an attack while on the battlefield, all allies are Fortified.\n\nThis unit can't have its Active Skills disabled by enemy passive skills.\n\nThis unit's attacks heal this unit for 100% of total damage dealt, will not wake sleeping enemies, ignore damage reduction effects, and any effects of non-boss enemies that would prevent targets from being defeated."
        }
      },
      "QueenyPassiveAMarieAntoinette": {
        "id": "QueenyPassiveAMarieAntoinette",
        "found": true,
        "localization": {
          "name": "Let Them Eat Cake",
          "description": "This unit enters battle Fortified. This unit cannot be sent to the reinforcements from the battlefield.\n\nIf this unit would be defeated by an enemy attack or a status effect while having more than 1 HP, it instead survives with 1 HP.\n\nAfter entering battle, for 100TU, whenever an enemy on the battlefield damages any allies with an attack, this unit's current TU is reduced by 50TU per non-burning unit hit. If this unit gets 3 turns within 10TU, this effect cannot trigger again until 20TU advances.\n\nEach time this unit takes damage from an attack and survives until after the end of the turn, this unit will heal for 50% of its max HP. Then, if the enemy team has 0 infections, a random non-burning enemy will be granted either the:\n- Lethal Poison status effect for 999TU, and become infected with it.\n- Cursed Sleep status effect for 200TU, and become infected with it.\n\nAfter the end of each turn, the granted infection will trigger to apply its status effect to a random non-burning unit on the infected unit's team that does not already have that status effect. Infection ends after 3 triggers (even if they find no valid target) or once the infected enemy is defeated or leaves the battlefield. Infection is not a status effect and cannot be prevented or purified, but the effect spread by the infection may be. A unit cannot get a new infection until their existing one ends. Lethal Poison deals 2 times the damage of normal Poison and ignores passive skills or effects of active skills that would prevent the target from being defeated, other than those which specifically prevent defeat from Poison or non-attack damage. Lethal Poison cannot apply to Burning units or Boss units."
        }
      },
